o worth  noting when Sam tells John about his  real heritage the two are standing in  front of Ned Stark statue in Winterfell  scripts remember the last time Jon saw  Ned he made a promise the next time we  see each of them  we'll talk about your mother that makes  it particularly fitting that John learns  the big news with a statue of his  adoptive father at his side Jaime  Lannister's returned to Winterfell was  bound to be a rough one after all the  last time he was there he tried  murdering a young bran Stark after the  boy caught him and his twin sister  Cersei doing things that twins really  aren't supposed to do as if that weren't  bad enough though he's guilty of  murdering Daenerys his father which  earned him the name Kingslayer suffice  to say he doesn't receive a particularly  warm welcome even after his friend  Brienne of Tarth vouches for his  character though he's granted a royal  reprieved by the mother of dragons it  soon becomes clear that he doesn't have  a lot of faith in his new queen and she  is different she is and srivasa I am  keep in mind that Daenerys his father  had a nickname of his own the Mad King  for obvious reasons Jaime has never had  anything good to say about it may the  skin blackened  melted of that bones no wonder he's  distrustful of Daenerys especially  considering her own fondness for fire  if Daenerys is poised to turn into the  mad queen as many fans suspect Jamie  will have been right not to trust her  only time will tell how all that plays  out until then we'll be watching closely  so closely check out one of our newest  videos right here plus even more looper  videos about Game of Thrones are coming  soon subscribe to our YouTube channel  and hit the bell so you don't miss a  single one  [Applause]  [Music]  [Applause]  [Music]
 

